# Command trufflehog

## What does this command do:

Find, verify, and analyze leaked credentials

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: curl -sSfL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/main/scripts/install.sh | sh -s -- -b ~/.local/bin
For Raspberry Pi install using: curl -sSfL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/main/scripts/install.sh | sh -s -- -b ~/.local/bin
For Mac install using: brew install trufflehog
For Mac container (Fedora Linux, ARM/aarch64) install using: curl -sSfL https://raw.githubusercontent.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog/main/scripts/install.sh | sh -s -- -b ~/.local/bin

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/trufflehog
For Raspberry Pi run: ~/.local/bin/trufflehog
For Mac run: /opt/homebrew/bin/trufflehog
For Mac container run: ~/.local/bin/trufflehog

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/trufflesecurity/trufflehog

## Command options

# Scan a local git repo
trufflehog git file://path/to/repo

# Scan a remote GitHub repo
trufflehog git https://github.com/org/repo

# Scan all repos in a GitHub org
trufflehog github --org=myorg --token=$GITHUB_TOKEN

# Scan a GitLab project
trufflehog gitlab --token=$GITLAB_TOKEN --project=myproject

# Scan local filesystem path(s)
trufflehog filesystem /path/to/scan

# Scan an S3 bucket
trufflehog s3 --bucket=mybucket

# Scan a Docker image
trufflehog docker --image=myimage:tag

# Output as JSON
trufflehog git https://github.com/org/repo -j

# Only show verified results
trufflehog git https://github.com/org/repo --results=verified

# Skip credential verification (faster)
trufflehog git https://github.com/org/repo --no-verification

# Exit with code 183 if any results found (useful in CI)
trufflehog git https://github.com/org/repo --fail

# Scan from stdin
cat somefile | trufflehog stdin

# Analyze a detected API key for permissions
trufflehog analyze

# Limit concurrency
trufflehog git https://github.com/org/repo --concurrency=4

# Include only specific detectors (by name or ID)
trufflehog git https://github.com/org/repo --include-detectors=AWS,Slack

# Exclude specific detectors
trufflehog git https://github.com/org/repo --exclude-detectors=Generic

# Filter unverified results by Shannon entropy (start with 3.0)
trufflehog git https://github.com/org/repo --filter-entropy=3.0

# Set log verbosity (0=info .. 5=trace, -1=off)
trufflehog git https://github.com/org/repo --log-level=2

# Use a config file for multi-source scans
trufflehog multi-scan --config=trufflehog.yml
